To load the files, load lisp/load-cl.el into Emacs.  Warning: Loading the
last file, populate.el, will take a while, especially on slow computers.

It's important to compile the files for improved speed.  To do this,
type "M-x compile-cl".  A Makefile is also included, so you can just
type "make" at a shell.

The code is verified to work with current GNU Emacs releases; run
"make check" (or "bash lisp/test") to confirm it works on yours.

To start an interactive session, type "M-x emacs-cl".

With the "emacs-cl" script in lisp/, it's also possible to run Emacs
Common Lisp in batch mode.
